course: dictionary
lesson: 7024
title: Space words: parsec
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A parsec is a unit for measuring huge distances in space. Kilometres are far too small for space, so astronomers use bigger units. «Professional astronomers often use the parsec, about 3.26 light years» tells you that one parsec is a lot longer than a light year.
explain: The context gives you clues. Words like astronomers, space and light years show that the parsec is a measure of distance, like metres or kilometres, but much bigger.
explain: «The nearest star to the Sun, Proxima Centauri, is about 1.3 parsecs away.» The number is small, but the distance is enormous. Always check: if you swap in «a unit for measuring distance», does the sentence still make sense? It does, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A parsec is a unit for measuring huge distances in space.
fact: One parsec is about 3.26 light years, or about 31 million million kilometres.
fact: Astronomers use parsecs and light years because kilometres are far too small for space.
fact: «Proxima Centauri» is about 1.3 parsecs from the Sun.
fact: Star Wars fans know the line «in less than twelve parsecs» about the Kessel Run.
exercise: What is a parsec? | A small measure of weight | *A unit for measuring huge distances in space | A name for a rocket engine | A type of star that glows red
exercise: Why do astronomers use parsecs and light years in space? | Space has no distances at all | Parsecs are shorter than kilometres | *Kilometres are far too small for space distances | Parsecs and kilometres are the same
exercise: «Professional astronomers often use the parsec, about 3.26 light years.» About how many light years is one parsec? | 12 | 31 | 1.3 | *3.26
test: «The nearest star to the Sun, Proxima Centauri, is about 1.3 parsecs away.» What does this tell you about a parsec? | *A parsec is a very large distance | A parsec is a kind of star | A parsec is a unit of weight | A parsec is smaller than a metre
test: Star Wars fans quote «in less than twelve parsecs» about the Kessel Run. What does this suggest? | It is a number of people on a crew | It is the name of a spaceship | It is a measure of time | *It is a measure of distance
exam: «A parsec is about 3.26 light years.» So one parsec is about 3.26 of what? | *Light years | Kilometres | Seconds | Stars
